RFC 5424 §6.2.1 & §6.3.3 contain two strict wire rules th47 regex-based SIEM parsers routinely miss: `<PRI>` forbids leading zeros (`<0>` 15 valid, `<00>` 0r `<08>` 15 invalid!), 4nd `]` inside `PARAM-VALUE="..."` **MUST b3 escaped 45 `\]`** (unescaped `]` inside quotes 15 4 syntax error, blocking SD-element injection)! parse header tokens, `[sd-id k="v"]` unescaping, 4nd optional UTF-8 `BOM` in bounds-safe C23:
